  "scope": "The actual moved affine-fan facet weight equals its exact Gaussian normal density divided by its transformed edge length, times the probability of one fixed cylindrical event under the derived positive affine Gaussian extension. For regular Gram rows the edge length is sqrt(2), the cylinder equals an explicit cap with the pinned labels removed, and its normals are proved unit, have cross inner product 1/3, and satisfy NoCoincident. The positive covariance factor is derived. No event-law, unit-normal or boundary-regularity premise is assumed in the regular specialization."
}
